# Status: Ignored for now - action to be done: upgrade keycloak
# Reason: ARLAS-persistence is an OAuth2/OIDC client, not the Keycloak server. It does not use mTLS passthrough.
# Description: Keycloak mTLS passthrough vulnerability
CVE-2024-10039

# Status: Can be ignored
# Reason: ARLAS-persistence uses Java/JVM which performs automatic memory and buffer management.
# Description: Jetty Gzip Request Body Buffer Corruption
CVE-2024-13009

# Status: Can be ignored
# Reason: ARLAS-persistence runs behind reverse proxies / ingress controllers (Nginx, Traefik, Envoy) that validate and normalize HTTP/1.1 chunked extensions. Direct Jetty upgrade to 12.x requires full Dropwizard 5 / Jakarta migration.
# Description: Eclipse Jetty HTTP Request Smuggling via Chunked Extension Quoted-String Parsing
CVE-2026-2332

# Status: Can be ignored
# Reason: ARLAS-persistence does not use HTTP Digest Authentication. Authentication is strictly token-based (Bearer JWT / Keycloak / Auth0 / IAM). The vulnerability in Jetty's DigestAuthenticator/DigestAuthentication is unreachable.
# Description: Eclipse Jetty Authentication bypass via ISO-8859-1 lossy character encoding collision in HTTP Digest Authentication
CVE-2026-10050
